/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-471-
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-472-Ordered by how directly the paper refutes or strengthens something landed.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-473-
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-474-1. **The provenance is env-specialized: make it model-compatible, or state where it stops** (Grädel–Tannen §6 p19, Prop 16 p23).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-475-   `provenance I env cs` (Closure.lean:240) drops every candidate failing `I.guard env` or `cost ≤ budget` *before* forming monomials.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-476-   - Build: lift the guard and budget verdicts into literals. Either env facts become tokens (the guard reads `E` through declared
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-477-     keys, see item 2), or each monomial carries a third component `envLits`. Then prove `provenance_iff` for **every** env, plus the
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-478-     update theorem: `provenance` after `Edit.apply` = `provenance` specialized (Grädel–Tannen Prop 15 shape).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-479-   - Theorem to add regardless: `provenance_env_specialized`. Exhibit an env edit after which a candidate becomes verified while
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-480-     `provenance I env cs` has no monomial for it. This makes the current boundary a tooth rather than a silent limit.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-481-   - Then **reverse provenance / repairs** (Prop 16): `repairs_of_provenance : ∀ m ∈ provenance …, applyAll (edits m) w ⊨ verified`,
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-482-     with the converse for minimal repairs. That is P4's "repair residual" turned into a computed object: the minimal token edits that
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-483-     would verify a hole.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-484-2. **Locality → minimality + early cutoff** (Mokhov et al. Def 2.1, §4.2.2). Today `locality` is a sufficient no-op condition and the
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-485-   comment admits it is not minimal.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-486-   - Build: a per-candidate **verifying trace**: the tokens `deps I c` *and* the env keys the guard read (needs `guard` to factor
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-487-     through a declared read-set, cf. `Frag.ReadsOnly` in Protocol.lean:561, which already does this for protocols).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-488-   - Theorems: `repair_minimal` (the re-judged log = exactly the candidates whose trace meets the edit) and `early_cutoff` (a re-judged
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-489-     candidate whose status is unchanged does not dirty holes that read its selection). Name `repair_agrees_from_scratch` as
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md:490:     **from-scratch consistency** in its docstring (Stein Thm 6.1; Adapton; Porter).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-491-3. **ATMS label discipline for `provenance`** (de Kleer printed ~p145; Grädel–Tannen Def 4).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-492-   - `provenance_complementary_dead`: a candidate with `t ∈ supports ∧ t ∈ blockers` is never verified (p·p̄ = 0). One line, and the
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-493-     disjunct-check reader will want it.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-494-   - `provenance_minimal`: absorption (drop m′ ⊇ m), proved to preserve `provenance_iff`. This gives the ATMS "minimal" property, and
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-495-     its image is PosBool[X, X̄].
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-496-   - Nogoods: a `conflict` status today carries evidence but records no nogood environment. Add `nogoods : List (List Token)` to the
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-497-     closure and `judge_respects_nogoods` (a candidate whose supports ⊇ a nogood is `conflict`, never `suspended`). This is ATMS
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-498-     consistency, and it is what makes P5's `refuted` constructible from *recorded* evidence rather than a fresh argument.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-499-4. **P1, guard as interactions: import incarnation, not only orthogonality** (Fouqueré–Quatrini Def 5.1 p24, Def 5.5 p26).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-500-   - Keep `tested ⊆ required → required^⊥ ⊆ tested^⊥` (cheap, true).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-501-   - Add `material T c` = the sub-filling visited by the interactions in T, and make `verified` carry `(T, material T c)`. The
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-502-     `gaveUp`/daimon theorem becomes: a filling whose material part w.r.t. a required interaction ends in the give-up placeholder is
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-503-     `partial`, never `verified`. This is ludics' own distinction, so the card should say so rather than present it as new.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-504-5. **P4, repair objects: change structures + checked transport**.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-505-   - Adopt Cai et al.'s change-structure laws for `Repair` (nil change = `kept`, `⊕`, `⊖`, `a ⊕ (b ⊖ a) = b`). `compose_sound` is then
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-506-     the standard `(f ⊕ df)(a ⊕ da)` lemma, not a bespoke axiom.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-507-   - `transported` evidence = the **re-judged** filling (PUMPKIN Pi's real guarantee is a re-check). Where a quotient equivalence exists
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-508-     (Lean `Quot`), prove transport internally (Viola et al.). Two evidence forms, `rechecked` and `internal`, distinct by construction.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-509-   - First-class substitutions (cv 01a1587d-9a98): scope the card to **context-morphism edits only** (`strengthening`, weakening,
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-510-     exchange), the class Cave–Pientka covers. Do not present token withdrawal as a substitution.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md:511:6. **P3, worlds: name them stable models and cite the TMS bridge** (Lifschitz Def C/D pp7–8; Elkan 1990; GMS 1993; Dannert et al.).
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-512-   - Restate `cycle_loses_grounding` as an unfounded-set theorem and `counting_keeps_cycle` as the GMS93 counting failure. Use the
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-513-     standard names and cite them in the docstrings.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-514-   - State `admissibleWorlds = stable labellings of the candidates' IN/OUT justifications` (Elkan). Then P3's union-not-a-world theorem is
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-515-     an instance of a known property, and the "analyzer has not finished" status is justified by NP-completeness.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-516-   - Before holes depend on holes cyclically: switch the provenance carrier to an absorptive semiring (Dannert et al.) or keep the
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-517-     dependency graph acyclic by stratification (Stein et al.'s unrolling). Pick one and write the choice in the card.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md:518:7. **P5, statuses and polarity**.
/Users/ember/dev/redregg/work/LITERATURE-CONTEXTUAL-20261020.md-519-   - `refines` as de Alfaro–Henzinger Def 14 (inputs ⊇, outputs ⊆) plus **substitutivity** (Thm 4), not only the narrowing
